INSERT INTO `intern_submission_report` VALUES (1,32,'','10','Interned at CRY, managing backend data for stationery and sports items. Designed Instagram posts via Canva. Participated in finance awareness sessions in Rohini schools. Listed schools in Delhi-NCR for internship outreach, connected with the government. school principals, and assisted in recruiting college students for internships.','','DS','delhi','Tata institute of social sciences, Guwahati ','Smriti Rustagi ','Social work','VE North Region ','','10',NULL,3,'2025-05-29',NULL,0,'2025-05-29',4,0,'','2025-05-18',''),(2,738,'','3','The work which i was assigned could have been better or could have been done more efficiently if there were better electronics and equipment and electronics. Due to old laptops, the work done was delayed alot.','','VE','Kolkata','Christ University Bannerghatta Road Campus Bangalore','Rubina Haque','Humanities','VE East Region ','','9,10',NULL,3,'2025-05-29',NULL,0,'2025-05-29',4,0,'','2025-05-29',''),(3,738,'',NULL,'\r\nThe work which was assigned to us could have been better accomplished or quickly if better electronic equipment were provided because if the software tools were updated, we would have completed the work more quickly','',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'','',NULL,3,'2025-05-29',NULL,0,'2025-05-29',4,0,'','2025-05-29',''),(4,112,'','','Interning with CRY has been a great experience. There were proper work allocation, but there was no feedback given on the work done. That could be improved. ','','VE','Online','Christ (deemed to be) University','Manoj Thapa','Economics/statistics/Mathematics','VE South ','','1,6',NULL,3,'2025-05-29',NULL,0,'2025-05-29',4,0,'','2025-05-29',''),(5,112,'',NULL,'It was a great experience. ','',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'','',NULL,3,'2025-05-29',NULL,0,'2025-05-29',4,0,'','2025-05-29',''),(6,610,'','','As part of CRY’s internship team, I led a fundraising campaign titled Hope for Her Education on Ketto. The goal was to raise awareness and support for girls\' education by sharing the campaign within my network, creating outreach messages, and encouraging donations to help underprivileged children access quality education.','','Communications','Online','NA','Manoj Thapa','others','VE South ','','6',NULL,1,'0000-00-00',NULL,0,'0000-00-00',0,0,'','2025-05-29',''),(7,432,'','','•Fundraising (₹16500)\r\n•Video editing\r\n•Volunteer for the Employee Engagement Activity at ARM Embedded\r\n•Anti-child Labour posts ideas\r\n•Researching about how child labour affects kids’ growth and socialisation and planning activities for awareness. \r\n\r\nHere’s the link to the images: https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/1ELGznEp3PY7OJFk5sVU9ze2-m2RkgUAO','','Communications','bengaluru','NA','Manisha','Law','VE South ','','4,6',NULL,3,'2025-05-29',NULL,0,'2025-05-29',4,0,'','2025-05-29',''),(8,371,'','','Employee Engagement activity at the ARM technologies office where in Employees enthusiastically took part in brainstorming and creating visually appealing and easy-to-understand flashcards. Each flashcard highlighted a shortcut  with simple explanations and colorful illustrations. The idea was to blend fun with function – enabling children to remember useful tech shortcuts ,along with a fun bag packing obstacle game . \r\n','','VE','bengaluru','National Law University ,Odisha ','Monisha Murali','Law','VE South ','','10',NULL,3,'2025-06-03',NULL,0,'2025-06-03',4,0,'','2025-05-29',''),(9,350,'','','I was engaged in researching, documenting and carrying out the data analysis of the micro-volunteering opportunities held throughout the year by CRY. I was in \r\nengaged in  converting raw data into valuable information and actionable insights.  ','','VE','delhi','Nalsar University of Law, Hyderabad','Shreeya Datta and Smriti Rustagi','Law','HO','','1',NULL,1,'0000-00-00',NULL,0,'0000-00-00',0,0,'','2025-05-29',''),(10,371,'',NULL,'I was asked by my mentors to prepare a side deck on 3 topics , the first one was concerned with the May- June highlights for the South zone VE , 2nd one was about the Vol cycle- Rec, Orient, Engage, Track again for south zone showcasing the progress we had done so far and our target statistics with a strategy for upcoming plans . Next , I was asked to come up with 2 activity ideas for the upcoming master class on cyber well being and awareness . \r\n','',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'','',NULL,3,'2025-06-03',NULL,0,'2025-06-03',4,0,'','2025-05-29',''),(11,15,'','1','I had to make an infographic for POCSO, Call up schools to follow up on YCC registration status, Give ideas for YCC Activities, Make the document of guidelines for week 1 and Assist with fundraising.','','VE','bengaluru','St. Joseph\'s College of Commerce','Bitapi Baruah','Commerce','VE South ','','1',NULL,3,'2025-07-01',NULL,0,'2025-07-01',4,0,'','2025-05-29',''),(12,432,'',NULL,'•fundraising \r\n•video editing \r\n•ideas for world day against child labour\r\n•research about effects of child labour on kids’ growth and future. \r\n•ideas on spreading awareness on the same. \r\n\r\nlink the vids and pics: https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/1ELGznEp3PY7OJFk5sVU9ze2-m2RkgUAO','',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'','',NULL,3,'0000-00-00',NULL,0,'0000-00-00',0,0,'','2025-05-29',''),(13,308,'','1','Assignments privided entailed different types of work from doing artwork to researching how women, children, marginalised communities are affected by climate change and finding way to implement awareness and movements in rural areas as well as social media. I also participated in an on field activity that partnered with an organisation to provide resources like bags and stationary to promote and help children’s education\r\nhttps://drive.google.com/drive/folders/15YgiWXUY6054twKyVraJXOxoigisOyd6','','Communications','bengaluru','Christ University, Dharmaram College, Hosur Main Road, Bhavani Nagar, post, Bengaluru','Manisha','others','VE South ','','1,4',NULL,3,'2025-06-03',NULL,0,'2025-06-03',4,0,'','2025-05-30',''),(14,670,'','','At CRY, I, along with my co-member Akshita, surveyed 240 past volunteers and 49 under-18 volunteers via calls and texts. We split the list—one from ascending, the other from descending order. Data was organized in a spreadsheet, marking completed, incomplete, and non-applicable responses. This experience improved my confidence in outreach, helping me grow more comfortable initiating conversations with strangers and managing structured data collection.','','others','bengaluru','St. Teresa\'s College, Ernakulam, Kochi, Kerala','Manoj Thapa and Monisha Murali','Humanities','VE South ','','10',NULL,3,'2025-06-10',NULL,0,'2025-06-10',4,0,'','2025-05-30',''),(15,670,'',NULL,'At CRY, my co-member Akshita and I conducted a survey of 240 former volunteers and 49 under-18 volunteers through phone calls and text messages. We divided the list—one taking names from the top, the other from the bottom. We recorded the responses in structured spreadsheet, categorizing them as completed, incomplete, or not applicable. This experience greatly boosted my confidence in reaching out to unfamiliar individuals and strengthened my skills in organized data handling and communication.','',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'','',NULL,3,'2025-06-10',NULL,0,'2025-06-10',4,0,'','2025-05-30',''),(16,610,'',NULL,'As part of CRY’s internship program, I led a fundraising campaign titled Hope for Her Education on Ketto. My responsibilities included promoting the campaign within my network, creating outreach content, and raising awareness about girls’ education. While it was rewarding, I had expected to contribute more in content writing, which was my area of interest. The experience could be improved by assigning diverse tasks to interns based on their interests and skills.','',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'','',NULL,1,'0000-00-00',NULL,0,'0000-00-00',0,0,'','2025-05-30',''),(17,368,'','1','I was assisting the Salem People Trust (through Child Right and You) in 2 projects\r\n1. Analysing the Health and Nutrition of children under 3 years of age in rural parts of Dharmapuri District.\r\n2. A study on the nutritional and educational status of children aged 0-18 years in migrant families of 15 villages in Dharmapuri District','','DS','Online','NA','Kaveri Krishnan','others','VE South ','','1,2',NULL,3,'2025-06-03',NULL,0,'2025-06-03',4,0,'','2025-05-30',''),(18,100,'','1','Research on MARQUEE colleges in Bangalore','','VE','Online','CHRIST (Deemed to be University), Central Campus, Bengaluru','Manoj Thapa','Economics/statistics/Mathematics','VE South ','','1',NULL,2,'2025-06-03',NULL,0,'2025-06-03',4,0,'','2025-05-31',''),(19,100,'',NULL,'I was given a total of 3 tasks to do. They were all fulfilling and I enjoyed being a part of CRY.','',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'','',NULL,2,'2025-06-03',NULL,0,'2025-06-03',4,0,'','2025-05-31',''),(20,100,'',NULL,'Enjoyed working for CRY. Aiming to work on-site next.','',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'','',NULL,2,'2025-06-03',NULL,0,'2025-06-03',4,0,'','2025-05-31',''),(21,100,'',NULL,'Attached ','',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'','',NULL,2,'2025-06-12',NULL,0,'2025-06-12',4,0,'','2025-06-03',''),(22,96,'','1','- Tasks Done : Made a report on the two (2) Bangalore Based colleges I.e Symbiosis & St.Paul college and How CRY FOUNDATION can meaningfully collaborate with them for fundraising and CRY Events. \r\n• fundraised more than 2500/- by becoming a supporting fundraiser in KETTO PLATFORM for the campaign .','','VE','bengaluru','NA','Manoj Thapa Sir ','others','VE South ','','1,6',NULL,2,'2025-06-12',NULL,0,'2025-06-12',4,0,'','2025-06-03',''),(23,598,'','3','I created a PPT on Child Safeguarding Policy of CRY and apart from that I also performed HR activities in which I assisted ma\'am in onboarding interns, scheduling interviews etc.','','others','Online','Loreto College ','Rubina Haque ','Humanities','VE East Region ','','11',NULL,3,'2025-06-06',NULL,0,'2025-06-06',4,0,'','2025-06-05',''),(24,778,'','3','Understood about What CRY India is and How it works for upliftment of our Society. ','','VE','Online','NA','Rubina Haque/Saumya Gupta','MBA','VE East Region ','','10',NULL,3,'2025-06-12',NULL,0,'2025-06-12',4,0,'','2025-06-09',''),(25,778,'',NULL,'Worked on working of CRY India ','',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'','',NULL,3,'2025-06-12',NULL,0,'2025-06-12',4,0,'','2025-06-09',''),(26,753,'','1',' I believe several areas could benefit from improvement to enhance the organization\'s impact and operational efficiency. Firstly, CRY can invest more in digital outreach and social media campaigns to better connect with the youth and expand its donor base. While the cause is noble, increasing online visibility through engaging content, storytelling, and data-driven impact reports can encourage more support.\r\n\r\nSecondly, internal communicat','','VE','Online','Christ banglore ','Rubina Haque ma\'am ','MBA','VE East Region ','','1',NULL,3,'2025-06-12',NULL,0,'2025-06-12',4,0,'','2025-06-09',''),(27,767,'','2','Worked at NAV Srishti (CRY funded) during their summer camp, toward their fun-based teaching for 4-15 year old children. I helped coordinate and run health camps, awareness activities for events such as Environment Day and Menstrual Hygiene Day, and other creative activities such as Friday Funday. I helped with the documentation of success stories of women who had gone through skill development programs, such as stitching & beauty salon, as well as successful implementation of the creche prog.','','DS','delhi','Nirma University Institute of Management  Ahmedabad ,SG Highway','Jitender Kumar Singh ','others','VE North Region ','','2,4',NULL,3,'2025-06-10',NULL,0,'2025-06-10',4,0,'','2025-06-10',''),(28,768,'','2','I had an internship with NAV Srishti, which was an NGO partnered with CRY, that worked on education, health, and social awareness. I taught underprivileged children, focusing on literacy, creativity, and confidence. I was involved in health awareness camps. I did many activities during my internship and planned events such as for Missing Children\'s Day, Menstrual Hygiene Day, Environment day.','','VE','delhi','Nirma University, Institute of Management, Ahmedabad,SG Highway.','Jitender Kumar Singh ','others','VE North Region ','','2,4',NULL,3,'2025-06-10',NULL,0,'2025-06-10',4,0,'','2025-06-10',''),(29,1361,'','3','While interning for Child Rights and You (CRY), I received a golden opportunity to \r\nprepare a PowerPoint presentation (PPT) on the organization\'s Child Safeguarding Policy. \r\nThis experience proved to be a valuable learning experience, since it provided an insight on the importance of child safeguarding and the measures that CRY has taken to ensure the safety and well-being of children. Moreover CRY\'s Child Safeguarding Policy, along with it\'s principles, procedures, and practices got instilled.','','VE','Kolkata','Lady Brabourne College, P-1/2, Suhrawardy Ave, Beniapukur, Kolkata, West Bengal 700017','Rubina Haque ','Humanities','VE East Region ','','1',NULL,3,'2025-07-04',NULL,0,'2025-07-04',4,0,'','2025-06-10',''),(30,1361,'',NULL,'During my internship with CRY, I had the opportunity to work on case story documentation, which proved to be a valuable learning experience. Through this \r\nprocess, I gained insight into the impact of CRY\'s interventions in the lives of \r\nunderprivileged children. I learnt to gather and verify information, conduct interviews, and \r\nidentify key themes and patterns. An idea of how to present complex information in a clear \r\nand concise manner was acquired. ','',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'','',NULL,3,'2025-07-04',NULL,0,'2025-07-04',4,0,'','2025-06-10',''),(31,1361,'',NULL,'While interning for Child Rights and You (CRY), I received a golden opportunity to \r\nprepare a PowerPoint presentation (PPT) on the organization\'s Child Safeguarding Policy. \r\nThis experience proved to be a valuable learning experience, since it provided an insight on \r\nthe importance of child safeguarding and the measures that CRY has taken to ensure the \r\nsafety and well-being of children. The whole process as well as the result \r\nwas new and refreshing to learn.','',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'','',NULL,3,'2025-07-04',NULL,0,'2025-07-04',4,0,'','2025-06-10',''),(32,110,'','11',' a pitch deck highlighting key child rights issues and scenarios in India, supported by credible data and statistics\r\nemployee engagement program at ARM\r\nImpact report 24-25\r\na word doc elaborating nuances of taxation laws, especially for an ngo\r\n','','DS','bengaluru','SREE NARAYANA LAW COLLEGE, Ernakulam ','M/s Subhashree ','Law','VE South ','','1,2',NULL,3,'2025-06-11',NULL,0,'2025-06-11',4,0,'','2025-06-10',''),(33,1976,'','5','fgthfyg','','DS','delhi','zdfghj','dfgfhj','Law','VE North Region ','','3,4',NULL,3,'0000-00-00','2025-06-10',0,'0000-00-00',0,1,'','2025-06-10','dfgh'),(34,1976,'',NULL,'decsc','',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'','',NULL,3,'2025-06-10',NULL,0,'2025-06-10',1,0,'','2025-06-10',''),(35,1361,'',NULL,'During my internship with Child Rights and You (CRY), I had the opportunity to work on case story documentation, which proved to be a valuable learning experience. Through this process, I gained insight into the impact of CRY\'s interventions in the lives of underprivileged children. I learnt to gather and verify information, conduct interviews, and identify key themes and patterns. Additionally, I learnt the vitality to maintain sensitivity for the children and families featured in the stories .','',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'','',NULL,3,'2025-07-04',NULL,0,'2025-07-04',4,0,'','2025-06-10',''),(36,1989,'','1','desfgdthfgj','','DS','delhi','dbththfg','rfgbrv','MBA','VE North Region ','','4',NULL,3,'2025-06-11',NULL,0,'2025-06-11',4,0,'','2025-06-11',''),(37,1989,'',NULL,'tfygjuhj','',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'','',NULL,3,'2025-06-11',NULL,0,'2025-06-11',4,0,'','2025-06-11',''),(38,1989,'',NULL,'wdaesfdgthfyg','',NUL