for tasks and updates, blend formats like videos and role-plays to keep learning engaging, and use weekly reflections for timely feedback. Partnering with more schools and sharing real stories on social media could widen reach. Focusing not just on tasks but the purpose behind them can deepen impact and build a truly engaged, empathetic youth community reflecting CRY’s mission.','','VE','Online','IIM Calcutta, Daimond Harbour road, joka, Kolkata','Smriti Rastogi','MBA','VE North Region ','','3,6',NULL,3,'2025-07-18',NULL,0,'2025-07-18',4,0,'','2025-07-18',''),(237,1138,'','3','This PPT outlines CRY\'s Child Safeguarding Policy. It covers the policy\'s introduction, implementation, reporting/responding mechanisms, and legal compliance. Key aspects include CRY\'s commitment to child rights, a zero-tolerance stance on abuse, principles of non-discrimination, and ensuring the best interests of the child. The policy applies to all CRY staff, associates, and external stakeholders.','','VE','Kolkata','Symbiosis School of International Studies, Pune','Rubina Haque','others','VE East Region ','','1',NULL,3,'2025-07-21',NULL,0,'2025-07-21',4,0,'','2025-07-18',''),(238,134,'',NULL,'Internship report','',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'','',NULL,3,'0000-00-00',NULL,0,'0000-00-00',0,0,'','2025-07-18',''),(239,1007,'','1','This report highlights Diya Agarwal’s internship at Child Rights and You (CRY) from May to June 2025, where she compiled data for the Talbros Impact Report FY 24–25 covering projects in Satna and Betul districts. She also supported an online education fundraiser via Ketto. Her work involved analyzing data on child health, education, and protection, and producing a detailed 9-page impact report. The internship strengthened her skills in data compilation, report writing, and fundraising. ','','DS','Online','Indian Institute of Management Jammu, Nagrota, Jammu','Deeptanshu Pandey','Commerce','VE North Region ','','1',NULL,3,'2025-07-22',NULL,0,'2025-07-22',4,0,'','2025-07-18',''),(240,1536,'','5','As part of CRY Foundation’s Volunteer Engagement Team, I led the World Music Day campaign—designing posters, managing logistics, and coordinating with artists and influencers to promote children’s rights. I also mentored 30+ interns, conducted 100+ interviews, maintained Excel records, and supported fundraising efforts. This experience enhanced my skills in leadership, communication, event management, and digital outreach while enabling me to contribute to a meaningful social cause.','','VE','delhi','JAIPURIA SCHOOL OF BUSINESS, INDIRAPURAM, GHAZIABAD 201014','MRS.SMRITI RUSTOGI','MBA','VE North Region ','','3,5',NULL,3,'2025-08-05',NULL,0,'2025-08-05',4,0,'','2025-07-23',''),(241,1465,'','1','During my six-week internship with Child Rights and You (CRY), I was placed in the Finance Department, where I gained hands-on exposure to the financial and regulatory processes that support nonprofit operations. The primary objective of this internship was to bridge academic knowledge with practical experience in managing finances within a social impact organization.\r\n\r\nMy role involved learning about voucher processing, financial documentation, and compliance mechanisms followed by NGOs in India','','Finance','delhi','OP Jindal Global University,  Sonipat,  Haryana ','Mr. Mohit Dhingra and Mr. Manish Khandelwal','Commerce','VE North Region ','','1',NULL,3,'2025-07-30',NULL,0,'2025-07-30',4,0,'','2025-07-23',''),(242,1465,'',NULL,'During my six-week internship with Child Rights and You (CRY), I was placed in the Finance Department, where I gained hands-on exposure to the financial and regulatory processes that support nonprofit operations. The primary objective of this internship was to bridge academic knowledge with practical experience in managing finances within a social impact organization.\r\n\r\nMy role involved learning about voucher processing, financial documentation, and compliance mechanisms followed by NGOs in India','',NULL,N